# Read by `alchemy` (deploy, dev, destroy) from the workspace root. Every value a
# Worker resolves with `Config` in its init phase is bound onto the deployed
# Worker as a secret, so this one file configures both local dev and deploys.

# Generate one: `openssl rand -base64 32`
AUTH_SECRET=

# Comma-separated origins allowed to call the API with credentials (ADR 0008).
# Never a wildcard. Under `alchemy dev` the website serves on 3001; after a
# deploy, add the website's Worker URL.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3001

# Provider credentials belong to `alchemy login`, which records *how* to get each
# one in `~/.alchemy/profiles.json`. Two methods, and only the second reads this
# file:
#
#   - stored / oauth — the credential lives under `~/.alchemy/credentials/`, and
#     nothing goes here.
#   - env — alchemy reads the variable from the environment, and it loads this
#     file, so this is where it can live.
#
# Which variable per provider:
#   Cloudflare  CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (or CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY + CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL)
#               and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#   Axiom       AXIOM_TOKEN (or AXIOM_API_KEY), optional AXIOM_ORG_ID, AXIOM_URL
#
# Two Axiom token types, and they are not interchangeable for deploys. An API
# token (`xaat-…`) is scoped to capabilities, and the stack needs org-level
# `datasets: create` and `apiTokens: create` to declare its own datasets and
# ingest token (ADR 0023) — an ingest-only token fails with `Forbidden: token
# does not have access to resource: datasets`. A personal access token
# (`xapt-…`) carries your full permissions instead, but is not org-scoped, so it
# **requires** AXIOM_ORG_ID — without it every call fails with
# `'X-AXIOM-ORG-ID' header must be set`.
#
# CI has no interactive login, so it always uses the env method.
# AXIOM_TOKEN=

# Per-stage overrides go in `.env.<stage>.local`, which .gitignore already covers,
# and are passed with `--env-file` — see `deploy:prod` in package.json. A value in
# the dotenv file always beats the same variable in the environment, so exporting
# it in the shell is not an override. Anything the file omits still falls back to
# the environment, which is why `deploy:prod` sources this file first.
#
# Three variables only make sense per stage, and all three are optional (ADR 0024):
#
#   WEB_DOMAIN / API_DOMAIN   Hostnames this stage's Workers serve on. Unset means
#                             unmanaged — alchemy leaves custom domains alone and
#                             the Worker keeps its `workers.dev` URL. Setting
#                             API_DOMAIN also changes the API's `url` output,
#                             which is what `VITE_API_URL` inlines. Never derive
#                             these from the stage name: `dev_$USER` has an
#                             underscore, which no hostname may.
#   SESSION_COOKIE_SAMESITE   `lax` or `none`, default `none`. Set `lax` only when
#                             the two hostnames above share a registrable domain.
#                             Wrong here makes every request after sign-in
#                             anonymous, with no error on either side.
#
# A stage that sets those also points CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS at its own website
# origin — the deployed origin is not localhost.
